  "id": "d9e800fe-a2c1-5889-a6d1-376ee1c71e22",
  "slug": "turkish-turkey-chili-pasta-recipe-11836730",
  "name": "Turkish Turkey Chili Pasta",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "This Turkish turkey chili pasta is Chef John's spin on the viral Turkish pasta, which is in itself meant to be a deconstructed version of a Turkish dumpling called manti. This is so much easier and amazingly, every bit as enjoyable.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Add olive oil to a pan set over high heat, and when hot, add turkey, and cook, breaking the meat into small pieces with a spatula. Once turkey begins to brown, add onions, butter, salt, and all seasonings: paprika, chili powder, cumin, black pepper, onion powder, garlic powder, oregano, cayenne, and chili flakes. Reduce heat to medium-high and cook, stirring, until onions turn translucent, and meat is crumbled and browned even further, about 5 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Stir in tomato paste, tomato sauce, and water, bring to a simmer, and reduce heat to medium-low. Simmer, stirring occasionally, for 20 to 30 minutes. Add a little more water if chili becomes too thick. Taste for seasoning before serving. Keep chili warm until needed over low heat."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Meanwhile, for sauce, whisk Greek yogurt, garlic, and water together in a small bowl; refrigerate until needed."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Bring a large pot of generously salted water to a boil. Add shells and cook, stirring occasionally, until tender yet firm to the bite, about 9 minutes, or according to package directions. Drain very well and divide into serving dishes. Spoon hot chili over pasta. Spoon yogurt garlic sauce on top, and sprinkle with parsley and mint."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 4,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 40,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 15,
